        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>BRIDLE T</strong> hree Hebrew words are thus rendered in the Authorized Version. (1.) Hebrews mahsom’ signifies a muzzle or halter or bridle, by which the rider governs his horse (Psalm 39:1). (2.) Me’theg, rendered also “bit” in Psalm 32:9, which is its proper meaning. Found in 2 Kings 19:28, where the restraints of God’s providence are metaphorically styled his “bridle” and “hook.” God’s placing a “bridle in the jaws of the people” (Isaiah 30:28; 37:29) signifies his preventing the…",
